{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "05JN", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-locally-projective}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2c0fd2c0bbc2b121a8770757666923e2bb4b1c1a6261e43cc55d6283ce388004", "source_text": "Locally projective modules", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b611e081fc66575efb185416f616dc98d8121665d1209d7c6a038dac714fe108", "unit_id": "tag:05JN:title"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05JN", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:01ec901fc8b72f47730207444dd2988a56512adbf0173e9d8656dfa5246a0280", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nA consequence of the work done in the algebra chapter is that it\nmakes sense to define a locally projective module as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fad530e1c28cc9f5320db1d3e0d360699217d5c2462b2d5f4a68624f177e98cf", "unit_id": "tag:05JN:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "05JN", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}(U)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-locally-projective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f31ba26002736cffdff802e6f394e2b10b5ab3d1e69996502a475282f6a5f211", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:16864d1b85727ea7cf180e284b576d7d0f4a6b4976cb7c75cd3a88ce9719e993", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0003>-module. We say <MATH_0004> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>locally projective<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif for every affine open <MATH_0005> the <MATH_0006>-module\n<MATH_0007> is projective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6c2263c5ec7c10c0acb174a8cd8907d69472fab215cde4f85bb75f5229c3aa26", "unit_id": "tag:05JP:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05JN", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}(U_i)$", "MATH_0008": "$i$", "MATH_0009": "$X = \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F} = \\widetilde{M}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0012": "$M$", "MATH_0013": "$A$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-projective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a677d3cbb64e541a8f952ca39ab7df2d840215bfaa6f91277a1b9f6ba275b764", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c02eb7aea0f308705eee6cbf2351e4e152da31c50436b4706cef66227eb7d10a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent <MATH_0003>-module.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is locally projective, and\n<STRUCT_0003> there exists an affine open covering <MATH_0005>\nsuch that the <MATH_0006>-module\n<MATH_0007> is projective for every <MATH_0008>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nIn particular, if <MATH_0009> and <MATH_0010>\nthen <MATH_0011> is locally projective if and only if <MATH_0012> is a projective\n<MATH_0013>-module.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:abe37e4762dd381b258f3149959e3b24a8cbdacb6c4d93b92464c7adda39deae", "unit_id": "tag:05JQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05JN", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$M$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0004": "$M \\otimes_A B$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0009": "$D(f)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}(D(f))$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(D(f))$", "MATH_0012": "$f \\in \\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0013": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0014": "$U = \\bigcup_{j = 1, \\ldots, m} D(f_j)$", "MATH_0015": "$D(f_j)$", "MATH_0016": "$j$", "MATH_0017": "$D(f_j)$", "MATH_0018": "$U_i$", "MATH_0019": "$A = \\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0020": "$M$", "MATH_0021": "$A$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{F}|_U$", "MATH_0023": "$M$", "MATH_0024": "$M_{f_j}$", "MATH_0025": "$A_{f_j}$", "MATH_0026": "$A \\to B = \\prod A_{f_j}$", "MATH_0027": "$M \\otimes_A B$", "MATH_0028": "$B$", "MATH_0029": "$M$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-ascend-properties-modules}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-standard-open-two-affines}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-theorem-ffdescent-projectivity}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b6c7a9a9b9e62992fe53fe3c1e77589075da4b56e681dc6816c92db2646ab418", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d81f19b658e085039a34366cadf7f4bde720c0c5914e6d186be94c21510f1c5d", "source_text": "First, note that if <MATH_0001> is a projective <MATH_0002>-module and <MATH_0003> is a\nring map, then <MATH_0004> is a projective <MATH_0005>-module, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nHence if <MATH_0006> is an affine open such that <MATH_0007> is a projective\n<MATH_0008>-module, then the standard open <MATH_0009> is an\naffine open such that <MATH_0010> is a projective\n<MATH_0011>-module for all <MATH_0012>.\nAssume (2) holds. Let <MATH_0013> be an arbitrary affine open.\nWe can find an open covering <MATH_0014>\nby finitely many standard opens <MATH_0015> such that for each\n<MATH_0016> the open <MATH_0017> is a standard open of some <MATH_0018>, see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nHence, if we set <MATH_0019> and if <MATH_0020> is an <MATH_0021>-module\nsuch that <MATH_0022> corresponds to <MATH_0023>, then we see that\n<MATH_0024> is a projective <MATH_0025>-module. It follows that\n<MATH_0026> is a faithfully flat ring map\nsuch that <MATH_0027> is a projective <MATH_0028>-module.\nHence <MATH_0029> is projective by\nAlgebra, Theorem <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:372af7725cc072f0bb5d157246ac3a71dad99963c39ec0cc42dda9fa95b7d404", "unit_id": "tag:05JQ:proof"}
